---
description: Repo layout, naming, structs, sqlc, proto, errors, PR gates
globs: **/*.go, **/*.lua, internal/**/queries/*.sql
alwaysApply: false
---

Apply when editing Go, Lua, or sqlc SQL.

Layout

- One package per functional domain under `internal/<name>/`. Follow `structure.mdc` for current layout.
- Allowed subdirs: `db/`, `queries/`, `migrations/`, `pb/` (generated), and domain-specific sub-slices (e.g. `internal/fraud/admin/`).
- Banned: `dto/`, `usecase/`, `providers/`, `repositories/` ceremony.
- `cmd/<binary>/main.go` wires config and modules only; no business logic in `main`.
- `pkg/` has no `internal/` imports. `internal/domain` (formerly `campaignmodel`) is shared hot-path vocabulary only (no json/db tags).

Files

- snake_case: `<domain>_<rest>.go` (e.g. `track_core.go`, `service_campaigns.go`).
- Split near 500 lines or when transport mixes with core logic.
- Tests: `*_test.go`, `*_bench_test.go`, `*_fault_test.go` beside code.

Types and tags

- Hot path: `internal/campaignmodel` — no struct tags.
- sqlc rows: `internal/<svc>/db` — `db.Campaign`.
- Admin JSON: `FooDTO` with `json:"snake_case"` in handler/service files.
- Replica/pubsub: `fooReplicaDTO` with json tags near serialization.
- Map at I/O boundary in one step: `db.Row -> toFooDTO()` or `db.Row -> campaignmodel.Campaign` (registry). Banned: parallel Entity/Model/View for the same table.

Errors

- Hot path (`internal/ingestion`, `internal/rtb`): typed rejects (`NoBidReason`, `filterRejectKind`), pre-built response bytes; no `fmt.Errorf` on `/track`; no dynamic Prometheus labels.
- Cold path: sentinels in `errors.go`, `fmt.Errorf("...: %w", err)`, `errors.Is` at HTTP boundary via `mapServiceError` / `writeServiceError`.
- Hot path wins over idiomatic Go where they conflict (`core.mdc` SLA).

Codegen

- `make gen` / `make proto` -> `scripts/ci/gen.sh` -> buf -> `internal/*/pb/`; sqlc -> `internal/*/db/`.
- After proto sync run `go run ./cmd/patch-vtproto-hotpath` for hot ingest paths.
- Do not hand-edit generated `*.pb.go`, `*.sql.go`, bpf2go outputs.

PR verification

- Hot path: `make test-alloc-gate`; benchmem 0 allocs on touched hot benchmarks.
- Cold path: `go test ./... -short` for touched packages.
- `make lint` before merge.
- Perf-sensitive changes: `scripts/test/gate_run.sh` or CI `perf-gate.yaml`.

Banned patterns (cold path detail in `cold-path.mdc`; slop gates in `anti-slop.mdc`)

- Repository interfaces over sqlc, Provider/Factory maps, `map[string]any` JSON builders.
- HTMX admin fragments — JSON `/api/v1` only (`control-plane.mdc`).
